        assertEquals(1, lcs.length());
        assertTrue(lcs.equals("A") || lcs.equals("B"));
    }

    private static boolean isSubsequence(String candidate, String text) {
        int i = 0;

        for (int j = 0; j < text.length() && i < candidate.length(); j++) {
            if (candidate.charAt(i) == text.charAt(j)) {
                i++;
            }
        }

        return i == candidate.length();
    }
}
```

The algorithm runs in `O(m * n)` time and uses `O(m * n)` space, where `m` and `n` are the lengths of the two input strings. Since a string pair can have multiple valid longest common subsequences, the tests for ambiguous cases verify length and subsequence validity rather than requiring one exact result.

