Two ways it could fail under load:

1. **Row-by-row Kahn loop becomes very expensive.**  
   The function repeatedly does `SELECT ... LIMIT 1`, `DELETE`, and `UPDATE` per node. On a large or dense graph this becomes roughly `O(V*E)` work, causes repeated scans and temp-table churn, and can spill to disk or run until statement timeout.

