1. **CPU starvation from long numeric fields.** A request like `P000000000000000000000000000D` is valid-looking to the digit scanner and is walked byte-by-byte. Many concurrent requests can burn CPU on worker threads or an async runtime. Add a maximum duration-string length before parsing.

2. **Memory exhaustion upstream from unbounded request bodies.** This function takes `&str`, so the caller usually has already buffered the entire request body. Without a body-size limit, concurrent large payloads can exhaust memory before parsing rejects them. Enforce request-body limits and timeouts at the HTTP layer.

